sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-10--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-glue-10: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.55";
    dc:description "Whether head number varies at a fixed genotype is an empirical contrast, and the published physiological manipulations report one-, two-, and zero-headed outcomes from wild-type stocks. Those results are paper-level measurements, not a sequence-plus-phenotype matrix. The software metaphor adds no further observable beyond that genotype-phenotype dissociation.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Hold genotype fixed, by wild-type stock plus reversibility or by sequencing, and record regenerative head number after different physiological histories. One, two, and zero heads from the same genotype would support head number not being a direct function of the genome; a genetic variant necessary for each deviant head number would refute it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "History can include microbiome and chromatin changes that are still encoded outcomes of the genome's regulatory capacities.", "Wild-type is usually inferred from stock history and reversibility, not from deposited genomes of the zero- and two-headed animals.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.63"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.548"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-10--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2023-glue-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.5";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-10--grok>.
